No selective improvement in the useful range proved yet. Composite divisors in ordinary intervals may be accessible to reciprocal exponential sums: standard exponent pair (1/6,2/3) in sum exp(hx/m), m~x''^{1/3}, together with a truncated sawtooth expansion gives error x''^{2/7} (logs), hence existence of a divisor in that band in intervals of length x''^{2/7+epsilon}. This needs careful checking and literature confirmation. Such a theorem alone does not handle residual GAPs.

